1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:28,380
Chuck, get ready.

3
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:32,700
Sis, don't panic. There's still a chance.

4
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:36,540
Looks like it's neck and neck.

5
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:37,980
My Sister clearly won that.

6
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:39,420
Why?

7
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:40,380
Stop talking.

8
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:44,190
I... I'll drop out.

9
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,140
He's still standing there.

10
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,540
I don't want to see him right now.

11
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:58,200
Episode 27

12
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:03,900
Grandpa!

13
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:22,620
What I did really hurt Mini, didn't it?

14
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:25,980
Was I being too heartless?

15
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:28,380
The thing is, at that moment,
all I had to do was say one word,

16
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,300
and I could've helped Mini pass.

17
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:35,100
At the very least, I could've helped her get

18
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:37,980
a chance to compete one more time.

19
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:40,380
Leo.

20
00:02:40,440 --> 00:02:42,780
Do you still remember what Grandpa once told you?

21
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:47,580
The 5 Stages: "Learn. Master. Refine. Perfect. Transcend."
Do you remember?

22
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:48,990
I remember.

23
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,900
You said those are the Core Principles
of Mastering any Technique.

24
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:54,310
Then do you understand what they truly mean?

25
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:01,000
I think so.

26
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:02,430
When practicing a skill,

27
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:04,380
those are the 5 essential stages you must go through.

28
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,340
Just like Shawn said,

29
00:03:07,950 --> 00:03:10,620
if you want to elevate your moves
to the level of absolute Perfection,

30
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:13,500
you must first learn how to conceal them.

31
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,380
Become formless and shadowless,

32
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:18,270
and only then can you become truly unpredictable.

33
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,260
Exactly.

34
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:22,140
For Training a skill, that's definitely the right approach.

35
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:25,020
But if you want to be a person of integrity,

36
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:27,900
this method is the complete opposite.

37
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:29,820
Do you understand?

38
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:37,020
You're saying that a person shouldn't
be too slick and cunning,

39
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:40,860
but should be a little more straightforward,
a little more honest.

40
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:43,740
It seems you understand. Alright,

41
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:47,580
we should head back now.

42
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,150
Grandpa, you go on ahead.

43
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:51,900
I want to sit here a little longer.

44
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,140
I'm heading back first. Come back early, okay?

45
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:29,340
Are you waiting for me?

46
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,260
Yeah, I'm waiting for you.

47
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,660
You waited for me at the Falcon Camp entrance,

48
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,060
Can't I wait for you here?

49
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:45,180
I never imagined you'd make a decision like this.

50
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:49,020
I had to do this.

51
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,900
I figure, if you were the Captain,

52
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:54,300
you'd make the same choice.

53
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,180
Not necessarily.

54
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:01,020
If Mini treated me the way she treats you...

55
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,860
I might have chosen to help her.

56
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,700
I don't believe that's what you really think.

57
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:11,860
Mark, Knowing you the way I do,

58
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:13,490
your sense of responsibility

59
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:16,380
would have made you make the right decision in the end.

60
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:19,260
You sure have a lot of faith in me.

61
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:21,660
But even so,

62
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:24,540
I still couldn't be a good Captain.

63
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,940
You've always been a great Captain.

64
00:05:34,780 --> 00:05:37,980
Honestly, I don't know what I would've done.

65
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:39,420
Maybe you're right.

66
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:42,300
Leo.

67
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:45,660
I saw everything last night.

68
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:49,980
I know you're hurting even more than Mini is.

69
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:54,780
Everything will pass.

70
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:59,580
I think Mini will come to understand it herself, too.

71
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,860
Oh, and by the way,

72
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:09,180
you're honestly more suited to be Captain than I am.

73
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:12,060
Being Captain or not really isn't what's important.

74
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:13,980
What matters most right now

75
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:15,900
is being able to stay together with everyone,

76
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,820
fighting for the Championship together.

77
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,180
This feels completely different

78
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:24,540
from any Competition I ever had back in America.

79
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:27,900
I'm telling you,

80
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:31,260
the Championship will definitely
belong to the Jianghai Team.

81
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:33,180
At least,

82
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:36,540
I'll do everything I can to help you.

83
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,820
No, to help the Jianghai Team.

84
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:57,740
Hit, hit, hit!

85
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:00,060
Take this!

86
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:01,950
Chuck!

87
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:02,460
Chuck!

88
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:04,380
Give it back!

89
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:05,820
Chuck, stop playing around.

90
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:08,530
What do you want? It's none of your business.

91
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:10,140
Give it here!

92
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,510
Chuck, you got cut from the Team.

93
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:13,980
We're all really upset about it,

94
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:15,390
But...

95
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,340
but you can't just hide out in the arcade forever.

96
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:18,780
What's it to you?

97
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:20,190
Are you gonna give it back or not?

98
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,050
Chuck!

99
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:22,140
Are you gonna give it back or not?

100
00:07:22,350 --> 00:07:23,580
Chuck, I'm begging you.

101
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:25,020
If you won't give it back, I'm leaving.

102
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:26,460
Chuck!

103
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:45,630
Mickey, have you seen my lubricant?

104
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:46,620
Nope.

105
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:48,510
Are you still mad at me?

106
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:49,500
Go away, shoo.

107
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,380
Why are you taking it out on me?

108
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,140
When I used to take breaks before,

109
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:01,020
I'd always grab snacks from Chuck to refuel.
Now that he's not here,

110
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:02,940
it honestly feels kind of strange.

111
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:04,860
I'm just not used to it.

112
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:07,740
Now I come to practice all alone,

113
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:09,660
and when I'm walking down the street,

114
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:12,060
I just feel so... lonely.

115
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:13,950
I was just thinking,

116
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:15,870
if only my Sister could come back and practice again,

117
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:17,820
I swear I'd never be stingy with her again.

118
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,740
If she wanted to use my lubricant,

119
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:22,140
I'd give her as much as she wanted.

120
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:24,540
I wouldn't even bat an eye.

121
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,940
Your Sister would never use your lubricant anyway.

122
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:28,380
Haven't you noticed?

123
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:31,710
Every time the Captain does maintenance on his Yo-Yo,

124
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:33,660
he takes care of Mini's Yo-Yo at the same time.

125
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:37,020
Come on, Mickey, let's go practice.

126
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:32,700
Mini.

127
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:36,540
Could we... could we talk?

128
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:40,860
Mini.

129
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:42,780
Have you ever thought about it?

130
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:44,700
Actually...

131
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:48,060
The truth is, Leo's even more
upset about this than you are.

132
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:50,460
But he's the Captain.

133
00:10:50,620 --> 00:10:52,380
He has to be responsible for the whole Team.

134
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:55,740
I understand all those reasons.

135
00:10:57,160 --> 00:11:00,540
It's just... I've been Training for so long,

136
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:04,380
and then suddenly, everything just... stopped.

137
00:11:05,980 --> 00:11:09,180
I really can't handle it.

138
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:11,580
Anyone would feel the same.

139
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:13,020
If, back then,

140
00:11:13,690 --> 00:11:15,420
if Leo had announced that Monica
was the one dropping out,

141
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:22,140
what do you think would've happened?

142
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:25,020
Have you thought about that?

143
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,940
I'm not mad at anyone.

144
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:31,260
I only have myself to blame.

145
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:33,180
You could always come back and practice with us.

146
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:36,540
I can't compete in the Tournament anymore.

147
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:39,420
So what's the point of practicing?

148
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:41,820
Mini, don't think that way.

149
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:44,700
Shawn isn't competing either,

150
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,100
but he's still contributing to the
Jianghai Team every single day.

151
00:11:49,180 --> 00:11:49,980
Mini.

152
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:51,900
You could organize a cheer squad for us,

153
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:53,820
or even just help out with Logistics.

154
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:56,700
That would mean a lot to the Jianghai Team.

155
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:01,000
This...

156
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:05,340
All of this... it all came from Leo.

157
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:09,180
Whether you want to or not,

158
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:11,100
It's up to you.

159
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:13,980
If that's what he wants.

160
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:18,780
Hmph. I'm not doing it.

161
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:37,020
Sis!

162
00:12:57,640 --> 00:13:01,020
Can I... can I handle Logistics for you guys?

163
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:03,900
Mini, thank you.

164
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:05,820
But I think, aside from handling logistics,

165
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:08,220
you should also keep practicing with all of us.

166
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:10,140
Because if a Team Member

167
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:11,100
suddenly can't compete,

168
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:13,500
you could be our Super Substitute.

169
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:16,380
Yes! My Sister can finally rejoin the Team!

170
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:18,780
Mini.

171
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:20,190
Actually...

172
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:20,700
Actually...

173
00:13:21,540 --> 00:13:22,620
Actually, I've already figured it out.

174
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:25,500
Your skills really are better than mine.

175
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:27,420
Monica. Train hard.

176
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:28,960
You absolutely have to win that Championship.

177
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:31,200
Shouldn't we go find Chuck and bring him back, too?

178
00:13:31,810 --> 00:13:33,320
Yeah, let's go!

179
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:35,110
Let's go!

180
00:13:37,180 --> 00:13:38,940
Coach Tony, let me tell you,

181
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:41,340
This is just like doing Business.

182
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:42,780
We had an agreement, right?

183
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:44,700
You order the goods from someone,

184
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:47,070
but when they come to deliver,

185
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,060
you say you don't want them anymore.

186
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:49,980
You tell them to just keep it and use it themselves.

187
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:52,860
Think about how that feels.

188
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:54,300
Yes.

189
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:58,140
I understand. I understand.

190
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:00,060
You understand? You don't understand at all.

191
00:14:01,180 --> 00:14:01,980
Our Mini...

192
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:03,900
Our Mini did a whole month of Summer Training.

193
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:05,340
Suddenly someone tells her,

194
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:08,220
"You don't need to compete. Go home and sleep."

195
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:11,100
It's just like if after signing a contract,

196
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:14,460
Party A has already poured in huge manpower costs,

197
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:17,340
but then Party B just unilaterally cancels the Project.

198
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:19,740
What do you call that? That's breach of contract.

199
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,180
That carries legal consequences.

200
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:24,300
Yes...

201
00:14:25,180 --> 00:14:27,420
I do understand. I really do understand.

202
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:28,380
I feel the same way,

203
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:29,820
this whole situation...

204
00:14:30,560 --> 00:14:31,740
it's just ridiculous.

205
00:14:31,900 --> 00:14:34,140
So unfair. You know what I mean?

206
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:36,060
You got it?

207
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:41,820
No, I don't get it.

208
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:45,180
It's like this...

209
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:48,060
A Customer clearly orders my Fish Head Casserole.

210
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:50,460
After I go through all that trouble to make it,

211
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,820
the Customer says they don't want
it and want to send it back.

212
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:57,180
Tell me, how crushed do you think I feel?

213
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:59,100
Can you just let them return it?

214
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:03,420
No way. Of course not.

215
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:05,820
Now you're talking, Coach Tony.

216
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,260
Now follow the logic.

217
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:08,700
Our Chuck here,

218
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:11,100
he's just like that Fish Head Casserole
that's already been cooked.

219
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:13,020
You can't just send him back.

220
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:15,900
Chuck.

221
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:18,300
Fish Head Casserole?

222
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,700
They're totally different!

223
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:21,970
How are they different?

224
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:25,500
When food that gets sent back,
nobody buys it, it spoils.

225
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:29,340
After my son was kicked off the Team, he also spoiled.

226
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:31,740
Chuck, come here.

227
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:38,460
Before, he ate 6 buns in one meal.

228
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:41,820
Now, he can't even finish 3 buns in a whole day.

229
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:47,580
I feel bad for them too.

230
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:50,430
But there's just no way around it. Right?

231
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:51,420
Coach Tony.

232
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:53,310
Just a minute ago, you were being reasonable,

233
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:54,300
How come when it counts,

234
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,670
you suddenly don't see reason?

235
00:15:56,680 --> 00:15:57,660
No, no, parents.

236
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:01,500
Hear me out for just a second, okay?

237
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:03,390
It's not that...

238
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:07,260
It's not that I don't want to take
Chuck and Mini to the competition.

239
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:09,150
The thing is, the Tournament Organising Committee,

240
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:11,580
They suddenly cut the number of Participants.

241
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:13,020
There was nothing I could do.

242
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:15,420
I went to see the Committee.

243
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:19,260
I went from the lowest-level Official all
the way to the highest.

244
00:16:21,240 --> 00:16:22,620
Dear Parents,

245
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:24,540
If I had the power,

246
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:26,460
if I could make the decisions,

247
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:28,380
had you asked me to take them

248
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:31,230
to compete on the Moon, I'd do it. I'd be happy to.

249
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:33,350
Coach Tony, you've really let me down.

250
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:35,580
You are pretending to understand,

251
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:37,980
but I see you're just getting more confused.

252
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:40,900
In that case, let me lay it out clearly.

253
00:16:41,780 --> 00:16:42,780
If my Mini can't compete

254
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,220
in this Tournament,

255
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:46,510
then I will immediately cancel

256
00:16:46,920 --> 00:16:48,870
my Sponsorship of the Jianghai Team's Competition Uniforms.

257
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:53,820
Ah, Mr. Mi.

258
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:56,700
We'd already agreed on this.

259
00:16:57,640 --> 00:16:59,580
You can't just change your mind on a whim.

260
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:02,460
If you can breach a contract, why can't I change my mind?

261
00:17:03,180 --> 00:17:04,860
What?

262
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:10,620
Isn't Mickey still on our Team?

263
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:14,460
Mickey! Oh, right. There's still Mickey.

264
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:16,380
Fine. I won't make this hard for you.

265
00:17:17,020 --> 00:17:18,780
People talk about good faith nowadays, right?

266
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:21,660
So I'll be fair with you.

267
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,100
I'll sponsor half your Competition Uniforms.

268
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:25,470
But you have to make sure of one thing:

269
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:26,430
That my Mickey

270
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:27,700
must wear the Uniforms I sponsor.

271
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:31,260
Half the Uniforms?

272
00:17:32,860 --> 00:17:34,140
What kind of nonsense is that?

273
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:37,020
Yes, yes, yes. This gentleman here is right.

274
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:38,940
If my Chuck doesn't get to compete,

275
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:41,340
I'll definitely cancel my Drinks Sponsorship too.

276
00:17:41,580 --> 00:17:42,780
Dad!

277
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:43,740
Stay out of this.

278
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:49,020
You... How can you do this?

279
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:51,900
And why can't we?

280
00:17:52,060 --> 00:17:52,860
Exactly.

281
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:54,780
You can change your mind about an agreement but we can't?

282
00:17:56,380 --> 00:17:57,660
You're pulling the rug from below our feet.

283
00:17:58,120 --> 00:18:00,060
Kicking us while we're down? This is...

284
00:18:00,850 --> 00:18:02,460
Aren't you just burning your bridges?

285
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:05,340
No, he's biting the hand that feeds him.

286
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:06,780
Killing the donkey once the millstone's done.

287
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:07,740
Cooking the hunting dogs once the rabbits are gone.

288
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,660
Cursing the tailor right after putting on the new clothes.

289
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,100
Kicking out the chef once the Banquet's over.

290
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,200
Enough!

291
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,180
I haven't even seen those Competition Uniforms yet.

292
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:25,020
I haven't gotten a sip of those drinks either.

293
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:27,420
It will be too late by then

294
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:30,780
Alright, alright, alright.

295
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:32,700
Dear Parents.

296
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:35,580
I don't want your Competition Uniforms anymore.

297
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:38,460
And I won't be drinking those Drinks either.

298
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:40,860
We'd rather freeze to death, die of thirst,

299
00:18:42,180 --> 00:18:44,220
than break the rules this Team has.

300
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:49,500
Dad.

301
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:50,940
Mini.

302
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:53,820
Dad.

303
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:56,220
Dad, I've thought it through.

304
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:57,630
The reason why I can't compete...

305
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:59,550
It's totally because my Yo-Yo skills aren't good enough.

306
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:01,020
I can't blame the Coach.

307
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:02,940
And you can't cancel the Sponsorship.

308
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:07,740
Seeing you upset... it makes me feel terrible too.

309
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:10,140
Dad, I'm not upset anymore.

310
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:12,060
I'm a Reserve Player now.

311
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:13,980
I'm still a member of the Jianghai Team.

312
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:16,380
And I get to practice with everyone again.

313
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:19,260
What about me?

314
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,660
As long as you're willing to keep
giving your all for the Jianghai Team,

315
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:23,070
you can also become

316
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:24,510
a Reserve Player for the Jianghai Team.

317
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:25,500
Really?

318
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:26,940
Of course it's true.

319
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:30,300
Dad, don't give the Coach a hard time.

320
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:32,220
I want to be a Reserve Player for the Jianghai Team.

321
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:33,660
I promise you,

322
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:36,540
from now on, I'll definitely eat 7 buns in one sitting.

323
00:19:40,060 --> 00:19:40,860
Coach Tony.

324
00:19:41,220 --> 00:19:42,300
I'm sorry.

325
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:44,220
No, no, it's nothing.

326
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:45,660
It's all for the kids.

327
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:47,100
Alright, students.

328
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:49,020
You're all smiling so happily,

329
00:19:49,660 --> 00:19:52,380
you must know some good news, right?

330
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:55,260
Monica.

331
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:56,700
You guess first.

332
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:59,580
Do you know what good news I'm about to announce today?

333
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:02,460
No idea?

334
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:06,780
Then I'll be the first to announce it to you,

335
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:07,740
Okay?

336
00:20:08,280 --> 00:20:11,580
Your Coach Tony here, he's really something.

337
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:15,420
To fight for everyone's Original Competition Slots,

338
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:16,860
He spared no effort,

339
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:20,220
and went to the Tournament Committee and
spoke with over a dozen Officials.

340
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:24,060
From the lowest-level Official all the way to the highest,

341
00:20:24,220 --> 00:20:26,460
they all remembered what he said. He told them:

342
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:30,750
"The Students' passion for the Yo-Yo Competition"

343
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:33,150
"is like the flames at a bonfire party."

344
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:35,580
"It burns with so much life."

345
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:38,460
"We can't be the ones to pour cold water on it."

346
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:40,380
After hearing all that,

347
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:43,260
every single Official was moved.

348
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:45,180
So, the Committee has decided

349
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:48,060
to restore all the Original Participant Slots.

350
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:51,900
Every Team member can now compete!

351
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:57,660
Students, inspired by your Coach Tony,

352
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:00,060
the Tournament Committee has decided

353
00:21:00,520 --> 00:21:02,460
to change the name of this Competition

354
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:04,860
to the "Blazing Teens Yo-Yo Competition."

355
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:08,670
The Team that wins this Championship
will be awarded the glorious title

356
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:11,100
of the "Blazing Team."

357
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:14,430
The Individual Champion will be awarded

358
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:16,860
the glorious title of "Blazing Teen."

359
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:18,750
Yeah!

360
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:19,740
Blazing Teen!

